1
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:06,443
On the Portuguese coast, a museum
keeps a tank of cold water.

2
00:00:06,443 --> 00:00:09,210
The fish inside are a national symbol.

3
00:00:10,210 --> 00:00:11,260
And foreigners.

4
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:16,651
Atlantic cod has never
lived in Portuguese seas.

5
00:00:16,651 --> 00:00:19,390
Its range ends at the Bay of Biscay.

6
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:26,066
Yet in Lisbon's old grocers
it is stacked like firewood:

7
00:00:26,066 --> 00:00:28,390
split, salted, stiff as a board.

8
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:36,680
They call it o fiel amigo,
the faithful friend.

9
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:40,878
It is chosen by weight,
sawn into portions,

10
00:00:40,878 --> 00:00:44,760
and taken home to soak, the
water changed again and again.

11
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:01,540
Why a northern fish?
Because salted, it keeps.

12
00:01:01,540 --> 00:01:07,080
Five centuries ago it fed sailors on
long voyages. Then it fed everyone.

13
00:01:07,500 --> 00:01:11,060
Last century, a dictatorship
made it a national cause,

14
00:01:11,060 --> 00:01:14,026
sending fleets to
Newfoundland and Greenland.

15
00:01:14,026 --> 00:01:18,970
Men fished by line from small open
dories, and were gone for half the year.

16
00:01:19,400 --> 00:01:22,460
The dories are gone. The appetite is not.

17
00:01:23,200 --> 00:01:26,110
Today the cod comes from
Norway and Iceland.

18
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:37,908
On Christmas Eve, in many
homes, it is simply boiled,

19
00:01:37,908 --> 00:01:42,480
with potatoes, cabbage, an egg,
and a great deal of olive oil.

20
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:49,020
Nothing clever.

21
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:56,660
A fish from somewhere else,
made entirely their own.
